--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This package ships the open-source signal-extraction primitives, ensemble
combiner, calibration interface, and reference client for AI-authorship
attribution — a per-code-hunk classifier that estimates the probability that
a given source-code fragment was produced by one of a known set of AI coding
assistants, by a human author, or by some other source.

The package composes with @ariada/haes so that a posterior attribution can
be canonicalised (RFC 8785 JCS), signed (Ed25519), and appended to a
tamper-evident Hash-Anchored Evidence Stream. This composition supports the
transparency obligations on AI-generated content under EU Regulation
2024/1689 (the EU AI Act) Article 50, enforceable from 2026-08-02.

The package ships an offline-mode classifier suitable for air-gapped CI and
on-premise compliance use. Production-grade accuracy is achieved by the
hosted classifier that this OSS client targets; the OSS reference
implementation is intentionally a commodity outer that does not bundle
trained classifier weights, calibration coefficients, or the closed
validation-corpus split.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HONEST FRAMING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Methodology validation across a large multi-language, multi-model corpus is
not the same as end-to-end production accuracy on real customer code. The
published research signal is not deployment telemetry. Customer-pilot
validation runs are planned and any production-accuracy claims are gated on
those pilots.

